From: Ralf Erlebach <ralf@example.org>
Subject: [PATCH] Make the behaviour selectable and stop including a core file

Two defects, both found by running local_stackmathgame's Behat and PHPUnit
suites against a tree with this plugin installed.

1. behaviourtype.php -- the behaviour is not selectable.

question_behaviour_type::is_archetypal() returns false by default and
qbehaviour_stackmathgame_type does not override it. Consequences:

  * question_engine::get_archetypal_behaviours() builds the list offered in the
    quiz "Question behaviour" menu, so a teacher cannot select STACK Math Game
    for a quiz at all.
  * If the value reaches quiz.preferredbehaviour any other way,
    question_engine::make_archetypal_behaviour() throws
    "The requested behaviour is not actually an archetypal one" the moment a
    student starts an attempt.

2. behaviour.php -- manual include of a core library.

lib/outputcomponents.php refuses to be included by a component:

    Coding error detected: This file should not be manually included by any
    component.
    * line 21 of /lib/outputcomponents.php
    * line 12 of /question/behaviour/stackmathgame/behaviour.php

The file is already loaded by lib/setup.php on every request, so the require is
both forbidden and unnecessary. With it in place no attempt at a STACK question
can be rendered.

--- a/behaviourtype.php
+++ b/behaviourtype.php
@@ -11,6 +11,18 @@
  */
 class qbehaviour_stackmathgame_type extends question_behaviour_type {
     /**
+     * This behaviour is meant to be chosen as a quiz's preferred behaviour.
+     *
+     * Without this, Moodle omits it from the quiz question behaviour menu and
+     * question_engine::make_archetypal_behaviour() refuses to instantiate it.
+     *
+     * @return bool
+     */
+    public function is_archetypal() {
+        return true;
+    }
+
+    /**
      * Questions can finish during the attempt, matching adaptive STACK flows.
      *
      * @return bool
--- a/behaviour.php
+++ b/behaviour.php
@@ -9,7 +9,8 @@
 defined('MOODLE_INTERNAL') || die();
 
 require_once($CFG->dirroot . '/question/behaviour/adaptivemultipart/behaviour.php');
-require_once($CFG->libdir . '/outputcomponents.php');
+// Do NOT require lib/outputcomponents.php here: it is loaded by lib/setup.php on
+// every request and throws a coding exception when a component includes it.
 
 /**
  * STACK Math Game question behaviour.
